[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799568289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105328#issuecomment-2799568289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105328","id":2799568289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m3gWh","user":{"login":"llama-nl","id":94882246,"node_id":"U_kgDOBafJxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94882246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl","html_url":"https://github.com/llama-nl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T03:12:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T03:14:57Z","body":" \n> Then, I want to load that file using: `FileAccess.open(file_path, FileAccess.READ_WRITE)` This is where I get **ERROR 7: ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND**\n\nThe error is wrong. @syntaxerror247 \n\n> This happens when exporting with no permissions. Because [according to android documentation...](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/shared/documents-files) my app shouldn't need any file access permission to access that file.\n\nYes, the docs say that you don't need permission for your own application storage, but must require permission to read or write internal storage, see [this](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage)\n\n> Instead, when I enable MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE permission, the file is loaded correctly. But I definitely don't want to use this permission, because any user installing my app could be questioning why on earth it's asking for full file access 😅\n\nYou can use [READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/Manifest.permission#READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE) or [WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/Manifest.permission#WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE) to read and write files. As previously said, to access internal storage  permission is required.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799568289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799801441","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105328#issuecomment-2799801441","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105328","id":2799801441,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m4ZRh","user":{"login":"edoartworks","id":18700548,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzAwNTQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18700548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks","html_url":"https://github.com/edoartworks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T06:43:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T06:44:21Z","body":"> but must require permission to read or write internal storage, see this\n\nYes I see on that page it says that **Documents and other files** (which is what I want. A simple text file) use the shared access framework and don't require permission.\n\nOr are you saying that txt files don't count as documents for some reasons?\nI also tried loading pdf files with the same results. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799801441/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800952106","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105328#issuecomment-2800952106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105328","id":2800952106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m8yMq","user":{"login":"edoartworks","id":18700548,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzAwNTQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18700548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks","html_url":"https://github.com/edoartworks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edoartworks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T08:59:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T11:13:19Z","body":"Update: \nseems like the issue is not related to the native FileDialog.\n\nIf I try to load the file by passing the path directly: `FileAccess.open(\"/storage/emulated/0/Documents/test.txt\", FileAccess.READ)`\nit still produces the same error.\n\nThe issue of FileDialog `file_selected` signal not triggering on certain folders, might be a separate issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800952106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880231919","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105328#issuecomment-2880231919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105328","id":2880231919,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rrNnv","user":{"login":"azuriancomet","id":181894976,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtd_QA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181894976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet","html_url":"https://github.com/azuriancomet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/azuriancomet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-14T13:22:33Z","updated_at":"2025-05-14T13:22:33Z","body":"Currently the only workaround is to create your own Android plugin and handle your external storage related stuff directly, using the Android API:\nhttps://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/shared/documents-files\n\nFor example you could transfer the file to the internal storage via the plugin, and then do whatever it is you want to do directly from Godot.\n\nIt is worth adding that requesting ```MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE``` _might_ give you some headache if you try to get your app on the Play Store, as per: https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/10467955\n\nThis is quite problematic for games that make use of godot's resource packs for patches or mods, as there is currently no way of loading those files without requesting ```MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE```.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880231919/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3011221612","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105328#issuecomment-3011221612","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105328","id":3011221612,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ze5hs","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-27T03:07:10Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T03:07:10Z","body":"> Update: seems like the issue is not related to the native FileDialog.\n> \n> If I try to load the file by passing the path directly: `FileAccess.open(\"/storage/emulated/0/Documents/test.txt\", FileAccess.READ)` it still produces the same error.\n\nFileAccess currently uses the MediaStore API internally so it has all the limitations of that, i.e without permission, you can only access files your app has created and is limited to Documents and Download directory. For eg, if your app has created the txt file then it would be able to load it without any permission.\n\n> The issue of FileDialog `file_selected` signal not triggering on certain folders, might be a separate issue.\n\nSignal is not triggered because that location is not accessible with the MediaStore API without the MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE permission.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3011221612/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3011248807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105328#issuecomment-3011248807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105328","id":3011248807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zfAKn","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-27T03:12:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T03:12:29Z","body":"Closing this report as it's a limitation of the API we're using internally, not a bug.\nSee the related proposal to fully support SAF, which would help to overcome these limitations:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12669","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3011248807/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]